  "known_limitations": [
    "Training data are three SYNTHETIC datasets (baseline.csv, enhanced_detection.csv, fraud_wave.csv; 120,000 records each; ~360,000 combined), generated by datasets/generate_dataset.py. They are NOT independently verified historical insurance fraud cases. Reported metrics are measured on synthetic held-out data only; they are NOT evidence of real-world insurance-fraud detection accuracy, are NOT production-validated, and must NOT be used as proof of commercial effectiveness. Per-country fraud rates reflect synthetic generator parameters, not real-world fraud in any country.",
    "Advisory fraud intelligence only. The model NEVER automatically rejects a claim, approves a payout, declares a customer guilty, suspends a policyholder, or makes a final investigation decision. All high-risk claims follow the existing human review / investigation workflow.",
    "Domain mismatch: training data is generic insurance (motor/health/property/life/travel/crop; 12 African countries; year=2024), while the live app is Zimbabwean life assurance with claim types such as Death Benefit / Funeral Cash Plan / Accident / Critical Illness. Unknown claim_type is ignored by the one-hot encoder; unknown country falls back to global statistics.",
    "Live application does not collect country on claims/policies; live 'country' is 'unknown' unless supplied, and amount reference falls back to a global (not per-country) statistic.",
    "claimant_age is imputed with the training median when absent; live value is derived from Customer.date_of_birth (when present) vs incident date. Imputation reduces accuracy for claims missing age/DOB.",
    "document_completeness_score is UNAVAILABLE in the live application; it is imputed with the training median (~0.77). The feature carries no live signal. (feature_status=unavailable_in_live_app).",
    "previous_claims_count live is derived from len(historical_claims) or a provided value; partial/limited history UNDERCOUNTS prior claims vs training. 'not_yet_calculable'/'derived' status is reported.",
    "reporting_delay_days live is derived from submission_date - incident_date (or provided); missing dates -> imputed. 'not_yet_calculable' when dates are absent.",
    "policy_duration_months live is (incident_date - effective_date)/30.4375, clamped >=0; synthetic training uses integer months 1..120. Missing dates -> imputed.",
    "amount_deviation_zscore canonical = (claim_amount_usd - mean[country]) / std[country], population std ddof=0, per-country reference with global fallback, fitted on training only; missing amount -> imputed.",
    "Missing numeric features are imputed with TRAINING medians inside the saved pipeline; this is reported via feature_status, never silent. Unknown categories are ignored; missing categories -> 'unknown'.",
    "Trained on a mixed-scenario synthetic pool (baseline + enhanced_detection + fraud_wave); prevalence ~13.7%. Threshold selection used out-of-fold predictions on synthetic data; re-tune on verified production labels.",
    "Fairness results are measured on synthetic data and cannot establish real-world fairness; country/age disparities require real labelled audit."
